# Copy to .env (gitignored) — `bun run tauri` is `dotenv -- tauri`, so these reach
# the bundler automatically. Neither key is optional for a build you intend to ship.

# Update signing. Ed25519/minisign, generated by `bunx tauri signer generate`, and
# verified against the pubkey in tauri.conf.json. Unrelated to Apple code signing:
# it proves the archive is authentic, not that the app has a stable identity.
# Unrecoverable — no later build could produce a signature installed copies accept.
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY=
TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD=

# Apple code signing. The common name of the certificate in your login keychain,
# created by scripts/make-signing-cert.sh. Leave it empty and Tauri skips codesign,
# leaving the linker's ad-hoc signature — which launches fine, but whose designated
# requirement is only the cdhash of the executable, so macOS drops the Accessibility
# and Microphone grants on every rebuild and every update. See docs/RELEASING.md.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="WhisperFree Code Signing"
# There is deliberately no APPLE_CERTIFICATE here. CI gets the certificate from a
# repository secret and installs it itself, and setting it locally would send the build
# down the Tauri CLI's own import path, which cannot resolve a self-signed identity and
# fails with "failed to resolve signing identity".
